DIRECTION AND TYPED SIDE RESULTS
a_meaning_in_b asks whether B preserves ALL of A's retained meaning;
b_meaning_in_a asks whether A preserves ALL of B's retained meaning.
These are not replacement direction names. Review every own unique span.
Choose exactly one result shape per side. Do not combine fields from different shapes.

COVERED:
- reviewed_unique_ids includes ALL own unique IDs, empty only when none exist.
- harmless_unique_ids is a subset of those IDs whose ENTIRE meaning is merely
  harmless UI, repetition or surface noise. A fragment containing any retained
  fact, policy condition or subject cannot be wholly harmless. Do not mark an
  entire sentence harmless just because it also contains a button.
- For every unique ID NOT marked harmless, opposite_support_ids must cite actual
  opposite/shared semantic counterparts and the explanation must compare their
  complete propositions, not just topics. Language difference is not a loss.
- When all unique material is harmless or there are no unique spans, opposite_support_ids
  may be empty or cite explanatory opposite/shared context. Such context is NOT
  promoted to semantic proof; the program records it separately.
- Do not output mode, loss type, source/counterpart witness or consequence fields
  for this branch. The program derives the mode and inactive fields from this result.

UNCOVERED:
- reviewed_unique_ids still includes ALL own unique IDs. Briefly identify the
  actual missing/conflicting proposition, not a short diff fragment in isolation.
- source_span_id is ONE nonempty own unique ID locating the decisive loss.
  It cannot be shared, a range/list, a generated quote or an invented ID.
- counterpart_span_id is ONE opposite/shared ID actually compared, or empty if none.
  Select location only: the program extracts exact original text without correcting it.
- retention_consequence states the specific information/function lost.
- uncovered_type is MAIN_CONTENT for same-record facts/steps, POLICY_MEANING for
  non-main purpose/permission/obligation/definition, RECORD_IDENTITY for an actual
  subject/recipient/service/controller, PAGE_ROLE for an evidenced function,
  STATE_VERSION for factual state/version, MEMBERSHIP for actual members, or OTHER_RETAINED.
- counterpart_relation is NO_EQUIVALENT_FOUND for an actual omission. CONTRADICTS
  requires an explicitly contrary opposite proposition and its counterpart ID;
  absence is not a presumed opposite/default/click/event.
- Do not output harmless or coverage-support fields in this branch. Partial
  coverage does not erase a retained loss; the program derives NOT_COVERED.

UNRESOLVED:
- Provide coverage_explanation, any reviewed_unique_ids and checked_opposite_ids,
  and status UNRESOLVED. Do not add covered or loss-witness fields.
- This is genuine uncertainty, not a convenient negative or a way around hard evidence.

Use SAME_SUBSTANTIVE_RECORD, NON_MAIN_MESSAGES, DISTINCT_OR_UNBOUND_RECORDS or
